ID: harness
Category: harness
Check: version__should_list_version_commit_and_features

Breaks wtpool --version of the installed build: build.rs reruns for a release build only when the
HEAD reflog changes. A commit reruns it, an edit does not, so after an edit cargo build --release
keeps printing a clean commit line. Debug builds rerun on every build, as now. Tests the dirty
half of the new release rebuild steps (oracle change p0r4-release-rebuild).

diff --git a/crates/wtpool/build.rs b/crates/wtpool/build.rs
index 2b6f7f8..34f7753 100644
--- a/crates/wtpool/build.rs
+++ b/crates/wtpool/build.rs
@@ -6,7 +6,11 @@ use std::process::Command;
 fn main() {
     // An edit or a new file anywhere in the repository changes the tree state without touching
     // a file cargo watches. A path that never exists makes cargo run this script on every build.
-    println!("cargo::rerun-if-changed=wtpool-version-reads-the-tree-on-every-build");
+    if std::env::var("PROFILE").as_deref() == Ok("release") {
+        println!("cargo::rerun-if-changed=../../.git/logs/HEAD");
+    } else {
+        println!("cargo::rerun-if-changed=wtpool-version-reads-the-tree-on-every-build");
+    }
 
     let commit = git(&["rev-parse", "--verify", "HEAD"]).unwrap_or_default();
